   NAME

	VCMAILBOX

   FORMAT

	VCMAILBOX [ASCII] [SWAP] [FULL] [VERBOSE] <word0> <word1> ...

   TEMPLATE

	ASCII/S,SWAP/S,FULL/S,VERBOSE/S,WORDS/F/A

   PATH

	C:VCMAILBOX

   FUNCTION

	Lowlevel utility to send requests to the VideoCore via the RPi mailbox.

	ASCII   - Display the first response as ASCII string.
	SWAP    - Byteswap the response words, to cancel the byteswapping
	          done by the mailbox.resource (see NOTES).
	FULL    - Display all the response words.
	VERBOSE - Display more detailed information.
	WORDS   - A mandatory list of words to send to the mailbox.

	Without any argument, the usage is displayed.

	The options, if any, must be declared BEFORE the WORDS.
	The rest of the line is reserved for the list of WORDS.

	Numbers can be decimal, hexadecimal (0x...) or octal (leading 0).

	The trailing words of the last tag may be omitted: the request is
	completed with zeros according to the tag buffer size. For example
	"0x10002 4" is the same as "0x10002 4 0 0".

	To build consistent mailbox requests, follow this documentation:
	https://github.com/raspberrypi/firmware/wiki/Mailbox-property-interface

   RESULT

	Standard DOS return codes.

	0  (OK)    - The VideoCore completed the request.
	5  (WARN)  - The VideoCore returned an error.
	10 (ERROR) - Invalid arguments.
	20 (FAIL)  - The mailbox.resource is not available.

   NOTES

	This is a free implementation of the RaspberryPi 'vcmailbox' utility.
	This port is intended to run on AmigaOS with a PiStorm/Emu68 environment.
	It requires the 'mailbox.resource' present in the Emu68 1.1+ expansion ROM.

	The mailbox.resource byteswaps the messages between the 68k and the ARM,
	so the response words can be used as 32-bit numbers. A few tags return
	blobs, like the MAC address, that must not be byteswapped: use SWAP to
	read them in their original byte order.

	For further information, please see:
	https://github.com/flype44/vcmailbox
	https://github.com/michalsc/mailbox.resource
	https://github.com/raspberry/utils/blob/master/vcmailbox

   EXAMPLES

	Simple examples
	---------------

	> vcmailbox 0x00001 4 0 0        ; GET_FIRMWARE_REVISION
	> vcmailbox 0x10001 4 0 0        ; GET_BOARD_MODEL
	> vcmailbox 0x10002 4 0 0        ; GET_BOARD_REVISION
	> vcmailbox SWAP 0x10003 8 0 0 0 ; GET_BOARD_MAC_ADDRESS
	> vcmailbox 0x10004 8 0 0 0      ; GET_BOARD_SERIAL
	> vcmailbox 0x10005 8 0 0 0      ; GET_ARM_MEMORY
	> vcmailbox 0x10006 8 0 0 0      ; GET_VC_MEMORY

	> vcmailbox 0x20001 8 0 0 0      ; GET_POWER_STATE  (SDCard)
	> vcmailbox 0x20002 8 0 0 0      ; GET_POWER_TIMING (SDCard)

	> vcmailbox 0x30001 8 0 3 0      ; GET_CLOCK_STATE    (ARM)
	> vcmailbox 0x30002 8 0 3 0      ; GET_CLOCK_RATE     (ARM)
	> vcmailbox 0x30007 8 0 3 0      ; GET_CLOCK_RATE_MIN (ARM)
	> vcmailbox 0x30004 8 0 3 0      ; GET_CLOCK_RATE_MAX (ARM)

	> vcmailbox 0x30003 8 0 1 0      ; GET_VOLTAGE     (Core)
	> vcmailbox 0x30008 8 0 1 0      ; GET_VOLTAGE_MIN (Core)
	> vcmailbox 0x30005 8 0 1 0      ; GET_VOLTAGE_MAX (Core)

	> vcmailbox 0x30006 8 0 0 0      ; GET_TEMPERATURE
	> vcmailbox 0x3000A 8 0 0 0      ; GET_TEMPERATURE_MAX

	> vcmailbox 0x30009 8 0 0 0      ; GET_TURBO
	> vcmailbox 0x38009 8 0 0 0      ; SET_TURBO (OFF)
	> vcmailbox 0x38009 8 0 0 1      ; SET_TURBO (ON)

	> vcmailbox 0x30041 8 0 42 0     ; GET_LED_STATUS (Status LED)
	> vcmailbox 0x38041 8 0 42 0     ; SET_LED_STATUS (Status LED) (OFF)
	> vcmailbox 0x38041 8 0 42 1     ; SET_LED_STATUS (Status LED) (ON)

	> vcmailbox 0x30041 8 0 130 0    ; GET_LED_STATUS (Power LED)
	> vcmailbox 0x38041 8 0 130 0    ; SET_LED_STATUS (Power LED) (OFF)
	> vcmailbox 0x38041 8 0 130 1    ; SET_LED_STATUS (Power LED) (ON)

	> vcmailbox 0x40002 4 0 0        ; BLANK_SCREEN (OFF)
	> vcmailbox 0x40002 4 0 1        ; BLANK_SCREEN (ON)

	> vcmailbox 0x40003 8 0 0 0      ; GET_PHYSICAL_SIZE
	> vcmailbox 0x40004 8 0 0 0      ; GET_VIRTUAL_SIZE

	> vcmailbox 0x40005 4 0 0        ; GET_DEPTH
	> vcmailbox 0x40006 4 0 0        ; GET_PIXEL_ORDER
	> vcmailbox 0x40007 4 0 0        ; GET_ALPHA_MODE
	> vcmailbox 0x40008 4 0 0        ; GET_PITCH
	> vcmailbox 0x40009 8 0 0 0      ; GET_VIRTUAL_OFFSET
	> vcmailbox 0x4000A 16 0 0 0 0 0 ; GET_OVERSCAN
	> vcmailbox 0x4000B 1024         ; GET_PALETTE

	Nested examples
	---------------

	It's possible to stack multiple requests.

	> vcmailbox SWAP 0x10003 8 0 0 0 0x10004 8 0 0 0 ; get mac and serial
	> vcmailbox 0x30006 8 0 0 0 0x3000A 8 0 0 0     ; get temperatures
	> vcmailbox 0x30004 8 0 3 0 0x30047 8 0 3 0     ; get clock rates

	FULL examples
	-------------

	> vcmailbox 0x10002 4 0 0
	> 0x00B03115

	> vcmailbox FULL 0x10002 4 0 0
	> 0x0000001C 0x80000000 0x00010002 0x00000004 0x80000004 0x00B03115 0x00000000

	VERBOSE examples
	----------------

	> vcmailbox VERBOSE 0x10002 4 0 0
	> [05] 0x00B03115 ; Tag[0] Response[00] => 11546901

	> vcmailbox VERBOSE FULL 0x10002 4 0 0
	> [00] 0x0000001C ; Size (28 bytes)
	> [01] 0x80000000 ; Code (Success)
	> [02] 0x00010002 ; Tag[0] Identifier
	> [03] 0x00000004 ; Tag[0] Size (4 bytes)
	> [04] 0x80000004 ; Tag[0] Code (Success, 4 bytes)
	> [05] 0x00B03115 ; Tag[0] Response[00] => 11546901
	> [06] 0x00000000 ; End

	SWAP example
	------------

	The MAC address is a blob of 6 bytes, not a 32-bit number.
	Without SWAP the bytes are reversed in each word.

	> vcmailbox 0x10003 8 0 0 0
	> 0xFF015FE4 0x0000ECEB

	> vcmailbox SWAP 0x10003 8 0 0 0
	> 0xE45F01FF 0xEBEC0000

	The MAC address is E4:5F:01:FF:EB:EC (the last 2 bytes are padding).

	ASCII example
	-------------

	This option is currently only useful with the
	mailbox GET_COMMAND_LINE (0x00050001) tag identifier.
	The tag buffer size (512 bytes) must be large enough for the response.

	> vcmailbox ASCII 0x50001 512
	> bcm2708_fb.fbwidth=1920 bcm2708_fb.fbheight=1080 bcm2708_fb.fbswap=1
	> smsc95xx.macaddr=E4:5F:01:FF:EB:EC vc_mem.mem_base=0x3ec00000
	> vc_mem.mem_size=0x40000000  logo=black ps32

	(The output is a single line, wrapped here.)
